>what is the whole sort of general mish mash?
The Whole Sort of General Mish Mash, as Ford would tell you, is what everything
is until somebody decides otherwise: every way things might have gone, all piled
up together like coats at a party. It is a handy name for the sort of mess that
cannot be sorted, and a handier excuse. Do not try to tidy it. It has views.

